# ============================================================================
# TRAME EDGE BEHIND CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (Caddyfile.tunnel)
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
# --------
# Used by `docker-compose.tunnel.yml`. Cloudflare terminates TLS and
# `cloudflared` dials out to Cloudflare, so no host port is published at all.
# The tunnel's public hostname points at `http://caddy:80`; Caddy keeps the
# same routing table as the HTTPS edge (`trame-routes.caddy`).
#
# INVARIANTS & SAFETY BOUNDARIES:
# -------------------------------
#   1. `Two Proxy Hops`:
#      - Cloudflare's edge appends the browser address to `X-Forwarded-For`.
#        Caddy trusts the header from private addresses (only `cloudflared`
#        can reach it: no port is published) and appends the `cloudflared`
#        address, so the browser is the 2nd entry from the right and
#        `trame-server` runs with `TRAME_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=2`.
#   2. `Host Preserved`:
#      - `cloudflared` forwards the public hostname as `Host`, which keeps
#        the Silo SigV4 signatures and the WebSocket `Origin` check valid.
# ============================================================================

{
	auto_https off
	servers {
		trusted_proxies static private_ranges
	}
}

:80 {
	import trame-routes.caddy
}
